{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788116215,"nonce":"TdjEKETbBuncsYZpMeW0/LjKqT4=","message":"AMENDMENT from spike 0.1 (FINDINGS.md, git-bug 3fa4cf5) — orchestrator, post-gate.\n\nOne bench fact bears directly on this spec's `interactions` observer and its\n\"what does an opaque dialog report\" open question.\n\n**The modded-window path is exercised by real mods from day one, not\nhypothetically.** The bench carries Hospitality, Gastronomy, Storefront,\nCashRegister, Guests and RegisterLanes on top of all five DLCs — 38 active mods\ntotal. Those are exactly the mods that ship their own windows and their own\nletter types, and Factions/Guests is the first analysis target (M3, spec 5.2).\nSo the `{type, title, buttons}` opaque fallback is on the critical path, not a\nnicety: design it against a window one of those mods actually opens.\n\nLoad order is pinned in `profile/gen-modsconfig.py`:\nCashRegister -\u003e Hospitality -\u003e Gastronomy -\u003e Storefront -\u003e Guests, ahead of the\nalphabetical middle (alphabetical would put storefront before cashregister and\nFactions before Guests, and Factions declares `loadAfter` Guests). Worth knowing\nif a def-resolution question ever looks order-dependent.\n\nAlso: with devMode=True seeded on the bench, six\n`probably needs a StaticConstructorOnStartup` hygiene warnings are expected at\nevery boot (Guests x3, FSWA x2, RealisticGasses x1). They are benign and\ntriaged in FINDINGS section 5 — do not chase them from a serializer.","files":null}]}